The bug: `cart.total()` computed tax independently from `price_after_discount_and_tax()` using a slightly different rounding path — causing the preview price shown to customers to differ from the amount actually charged (e.g. $16.17 vs $16.18 on a $29.95 item with HALFOFF). The structural risk of double-tax also existed: calling both functions in sequence would apply tax twice. Fixed by making `cart.total()` delegate to `price_after_discount_and_tax()` as the single source of truth for the final total. Added `tests/test_issue_2.py` with 11 tests covering the rounding-mismatch cases; full suite green (46 passed).

