`price_after_discount_and_tax()` was calling `apply_tax()` internally, so any checkout or preview flow that also went through `cart.total()` (which applies tax on the post-discount subtotal) would tax the order twice — customers with coupons paid `(subtotal * (1-rate)) * 1.08 * 1.08` instead of the correct `(subtotal * (1-rate)) * 1.08`. Fixed by removing the `apply_tax()` call from `price_after_discount_and_tax`; tax is now applied exactly once in `cart.total()`. Full suite green (42 passed).

